Jayappa v. Shivangouda
, MR 1928 Bom 42 and Amir v. Mahadeo Persad, AIR 1917 All 104 are all cases where there was no personal liability at all. When there is no personal liability undertaken by the surety, the question of attachment of the other property does not arise. We therefore do not wish to go into a detailed discussion of these authorities.

